// An ordering comparison on the `count` output column.
//
// Ordering is defined on integers only. A decimal "resolves but fails the integer conversion and
// yields false" -- so the identical policy over a Long column opens the gate and over a decimal
// column does not. Our model ordered decimals by their scaled value until 2026-09-11, which was a
// wrong verdict; no corpus case compares a decimal with an ordering operator, so nothing caught it.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (s: Long). (
        formerly within 1h Anchor::Action::"Score"::response{ output.count: s }
        && s > 0
    )
};
